# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# boot.part -- A moulded boot over either end of a chassis
# Copyright (c) 2026 Jakob Kastelic

# The frame: x across, z up, y back, the front face of the panel at
# y = 0.  A stack of profiles seen from the front: the sleeve round the
# chassis end, open at the bottom in a gap; the recess over the Lexan
# overlay; and the lip over the panel, round the lip opening.  The lip
# face rises into six bumpers, two on each side and two halves at each
# of the top and the bottom corners, in waves: the lip is what a tall
# extrusion of its profile has in common with two extrusions of a wavy
# outline, one along x and one along z.  So the outer edge of the front
# is one smooth closed run, and one round follows it.  Screw holes,
# counterbored for the heads, go through the side walls and through the
# top and bottom bands.
#
# The boot is made for a mould that opens along y and parts at PART_Y,
# PART_GAP behind the counterbores of the screws, so that every hole
# lies on faces without a draft.  The holes lie across the way the
# mould opens: side pins make them, or a drill.  Ahead of that plane
# the outside has no draft.  Behind it the sleeve leans in by DRAFT on
# every side, outside and in the cavity, so that the outside shows a
# crease all round on the parting line.  Slots cored from the rear
# leave walls of about CW: they run along y in the inner faces of the
# sleeve and out at its rear end, and those under a bumper run on
# forward as pockets under it, whose floors follow the waves.  The
# lands between the slots bear on the chassis, and the walls stay whole
# round the screws.  The values come from the parameters of the chassis, in
# mm.  Build it with
#   extrude test/boot.part | bool - | fillet - | tostep - > boot.step

W = 339.09
H = 170.688
WALL = 6.35
FOOT = 5.65
TOP = 11
LIP = 7.62
POCKET_X0 = 65.1948
POCKET_X1 = 273.8952
COV_T = 1.6002
BEND_R = 0.762
BOOT_R = 12.7
SOFT_R = 1.016
OPEN_R = 3.81
LEXAN_X0 = 5.1522
LEXAN_X1 = 333.9378
LEXAN_Z1 = 165.7898
LEXAN_T = 0.3548
BOOT_L = 38.1
LIP_T = 3.81
BUMP_L = 25
BUMP_H = 9.34
BUMP_Z0 = 64.344
BUMP_Z1 = 125.144
SCREW_Y = 10.16
SCREW_DZ = 56.896
SLEEVE = 4.7625
HEAD = 7.62
HEAD_D = 2.54
BAND_X = 60
BAND_XB = 55

X0 = -WALL
X1 = W + WALL
Z0 = -WALL - FOOT
Z1 = H + TOP
XA = POCKET_X0 + 2 * COV_T
XB = POCKET_X1 - 2 * COV_T
RV = COV_T + BEND_R
LX0 = LEXAN_X0 - 0.2
LX1 = LEXAN_X1 + 0.2
LZ0 = LIP - OPEN_R
LZ1 = LEXAN_Z1 + 0.2
RL = 0.5
YR = BOOT_L - LIP_T
DRAFT = 1
PART_GAP = 1.5
PART_Y = SCREW_Y + HEAD / 2 + PART_GAP

# The outer outline, then the cavity: its bottom corners sharp, for the
# square edges of the front plate; the top ones clear the outer bends of
# the top cover.  The outline of the rear of the sleeve, backd, has the
# corners of the gap round, for a sharp corner would turn at the parting
# line, and no ball rolls round that turn.  The round shrinks with the
# draft, to SOFT_R less the lean at the rear end.
profile back along y XB Z0 0 X1 Z0 BOOT_R X1 Z1 BOOT_R X0 Z1 BOOT_R
corner X0 Z0 BOOT_R XA Z0 0
corner XA 0 RV 0 0 0 0 H SOFT_R W H SOFT_R W 0 0 XB 0 RV
profile lip along y XB Z0 0 X1 Z0 BOOT_R X1 Z1 BOOT_R X0 Z1 BOOT_R
corner X0 Z0 BOOT_R XA Z0 0
corner XA LIP OPEN_R LIP LIP OPEN_R LIP H-LIP OPEN_R W-LIP H-LIP OPEN_R
corner W-LIP LIP OPEN_R XB LIP OPEN_R
profile lipx along y XB Z0 0 X1 Z0 BOOT_R X1 Z1 BOOT_R X0 Z1 BOOT_R
corner X0 Z0 BOOT_R XA Z0 0
corner XA LZ0 0 LX0 LZ0 RL LX0 LZ1 RL LX1 LZ1 RL LX1 LZ0 RL XB LZ0 0

profile backd along y XB Z0 SOFT_R X1 Z0 BOOT_R X1 Z1 BOOT_R X0 Z1 BOOT_R
corner X0 Z0 BOOT_R XA Z0 SOFT_R
corner XA 0 RV 0 0 0 0 H SOFT_R W H SOFT_R W 0 0 XB 0 RV
extrude sleeve from 0 to PART_Y back
extrude rear from PART_Y to YR backd draft DRAFT
extrude recess from -LEXAN_T to 0 lipx

# The waves.  Seen from the side, pv, the front runs at the height of
# the bumpers, YB, for BLV from the top and from the bottom and between
# BUMP_Z0 and BUMP_Z1, and at the lip face, -LIP_T, between; seen from
# above, ph, at YB for BUMP_L from each side.  Each step is an S of two
# arcs, A1 where it turns outward and A2 where it turns inward.  Both
# outlines close behind the lip, at YE, and beyond the outer faces.
A1 = 5.6
A2 = 3.6
BLV = 30
YB = -LIP_T - BUMP_H
YE = 1
profile pv along x YE Z0-1 0 YE Z1+1 0 YB Z1+1 0 YB Z1-BLV A1
corner -LIP_T Z1-BLV A2 -LIP_T BUMP_Z1 A2 YB BUMP_Z1 A1 YB BUMP_Z0 A1
corner -LIP_T BUMP_Z0 A2 -LIP_T Z0+BLV A2 YB Z0+BLV A1 YB Z0-1 0
profile ph along z X0-1 YE 0 X0-1 YB 0 X0+BUMP_L YB A1 X0+BUMP_L -LIP_T A2
corner X1-BUMP_L -LIP_T A2 X1-BUMP_L YB A1 X1+1 YB 0 X1+1 YE 0
extrude tall from YB-1 to -LEXAN_T lip
extrude wv from X0-1 to X1+1 pv
extrude wh from Z0-1 to Z1+1 ph
common f1 tall wv
common front f1 wh
union bumped sleeve rear recess front

# The screw holes, each a sleeve hole from the outer face with a
# counterbore for the head.
ZS0 = H/2-SCREW_DZ
ZS1 = H/2+SCREW_DZ
circle side0 along x SCREW_Y ZS0 SLEEVE
circle side1 along x SCREW_Y ZS1 SLEEVE
circle head0 along x SCREW_Y ZS0 HEAD
circle head1 along x SCREW_Y ZS1 HEAD
extrude hl0 from X0 to 0 side0
extrude hl1 from X0 to 0 side1
extrude hr0 from W to X1 side0
extrude hr1 from W to X1 side1
extrude cl0 from X0 to X0+HEAD_D head0
extrude cl1 from X0 to X0+HEAD_D head1
extrude cr0 from X1-HEAD_D to X1 head0
extrude cr1 from X1-HEAD_D to X1 head1
circle top0 along z BAND_X SCREW_Y SLEEVE
circle top1 along z W-BAND_X SCREW_Y SLEEVE
circle tophead0 along z BAND_X SCREW_Y HEAD
circle tophead1 along z W-BAND_X SCREW_Y HEAD
circle bot0 along z BAND_XB SCREW_Y SLEEVE
circle bot1 along z W-BAND_XB SCREW_Y SLEEVE
circle bothead0 along z BAND_XB SCREW_Y HEAD
circle bothead1 along z W-BAND_XB SCREW_Y HEAD
extrude ht0 from H to Z1 top0
extrude ht1 from H to Z1 top1
extrude ct0 from Z1-HEAD_D to Z1 tophead0
extrude ct1 from Z1-HEAD_D to Z1 tophead1
extrude hb0 from Z0 to 0 bot0
extrude hb1 from Z0 to 0 bot1
extrude cb0 from Z0 to Z0+HEAD_D bothead0
extrude cb1 from Z0 to Z0+HEAD_D bothead1
cut holed bumped hl0 hl1 hr0 hr1 cl0 cl1 cr0 cr1 ht0 ht1 ct0 ct1 hb0 hb1 cb0 cb1

# The cores.  Each is an extrusion from YT, past the rear end, toward
# the front, which shrinks by DRAFT on the way, so the outlines below
# hold at YT and lie E0 further out than at y = 0.  CW is the wall left
# to the outside at y = 0, and CL that under the waves.
TD = tan(DRAFT)
YT = YR+1
E0 = YT*TD
CW = 4
CL = 3.5

# The floors of the pockets: the waves moved in by CL, their steps
# leaning by SD.  ARC is the length of a step's inner arc along the lip.
SD = 2
SL = BUMP_H*tan(SD)
ARC = (A2+CL)*tan(45-SD/2)
YD = YB+CL
YL = -LIP_T+CL
ZT = Z1-BLV+CL
ZU = BUMP_Z1-CL
ZV = BUMP_Z0+CL
ZW = Z0+BLV-CL
XU = X0+BUMP_L-CL
X1U = X1-BUMP_L+CL
profile pvo along x YT+1 Z0-1 0 YT+1 Z1+1 0 YD Z1+1 0 YD ZT A1-CL
corner YL ZT-SL A2+CL YL ZU+SL A2+CL YD ZU A1-CL YD ZV A1-CL
corner YL ZV-SL A2+CL YL ZW+SL A2+CL YD ZW A1-CL YD Z0-1 0
profile pho along z X0-1 YT+1 0 X0-1 YD 0 XU YD A1-CL XU+SL YL A2+CL
corner X1U-SL YL A2+CL X1U YD A1-CL X1+1 YD 0 X1+1 YT+1 0
extrude wvo from X0-1 to X1+1 pvo
extrude who from Z0-1 to Z1+1 pho

# The slots that run on under the bumpers: one round each corner of the
# cavity, lbl to ltr, and four along each side wall, psl and psr.  A
# slot reaches from CW inside the outer face to FIN short of the wall of
# the recess, across the back of the lip.  Its corners are round: CR,
# and CRS where the slot is shallow or a screw is near; RCI inside the
# corner of the cavity.  Two chords, with corners of RC, follow the
# outer corner round of the sleeve at CW.  The ends of the corner slots
# lie GAP past the steps of the floor, on its flat parts, since a round
# corner of a slot meets no step in a line or a circle.
FIN = 1.4
GAP = 0.12
CR = 1.75+E0
CRS = 1+E0
RC = 2+E0
RCI = 1.2
XO = X0+CW-E0
XI = LX0-FIN
ZO0 = Z0+CW-E0
ZI0 = LZ0-FIN
ZO1 = Z1-CW+E0
ZI1 = LZ1+FIN
RO = BOOT_R-CW+E0
S45 = sqrt(0.5)
CX = X0+BOOT_R
CZ0 = Z0+BOOT_R
CZ1 = Z1-BOOT_R
AX = CX-RO*S45
XE = XU+SL+ARC+GAP+CR
ZE = ZW+SL+ARC+GAP+CR
ZF = ZT-SL-ARC-GAP-CRS
profile lbl along y XO CZ0 RC AX CZ0-RO*S45 RC CX ZO0 RC XE ZO0 CR XE ZI0 CR
corner XI ZI0 RCI XI ZE CR XO ZE CRS
profile ltl along y XO ZF CRS XI ZF CRS XI ZI1 RCI XE ZI1 CR XE ZO1 CR
corner CX ZO1 RC AX CZ1+RO*S45 RC XO CZ1 RC
profile lbr along y W-XO CZ0 RC W-AX CZ0-RO*S45 RC W-CX ZO0 RC W-XE ZO0 CR
corner W-XE ZI0 CR W-XI ZI0 RCI W-XI ZE CR W-XO ZE CRS
profile ltr along y W-XO ZF CRS W-XI ZF CRS W-XI ZI1 RCI W-XE ZI1 CR
corner W-XE ZO1 CR W-CX ZO1 RC W-AX CZ1+RO*S45 RC W-XO CZ1 RC
ZP = ZS0+4.95
SG = 22.2
SP = 25.4
profile psl along y XO ZP-E0 CRS XI ZP-E0 CR XI ZP+SG+E0 CR XO ZP+SG+E0 CRS
profile psr along y W-XO ZP-E0 CRS W-XO ZP+SG+E0 CRS W-XI ZP+SG+E0 CR
corner W-XI ZP-E0 CR
extrude kbl from YT to YB lbl draft DRAFT
extrude ktl from YT to YB ltl draft DRAFT
extrude kbr from YT to YB lbr draft DRAFT
extrude ktr from YT to YB ltr draft DRAFT
extrude ksl from YT to YB psl draft DRAFT pattern z 4 SP
extrude ksr from YT to YB psr draft DRAFT pattern z 4 SP
union slots kbl ktl kbr ktr ksl ksr
common slotv slots wvo
common core slotv who

# The grooves of the top wall and of the bottom bands, between the
# corner slots and clear of the screws by BOSS: they end flush with the
# back of the lip, at y = 0.  LAND is the land between two at y = 0.
BOSS = 5.05
LAND = 3.2
GX0 = XE-E0+LAND
GT1 = BAND_X-BOSS
GB1 = BAND_XB-BOSS
GE0 = BAND_XB+BOSS
GE1 = XA-4.4
GN = 8
GP = (W-2*BAND_X-2*BOSS+LAND)/GN
profile pgt along y GX0-E0 H-1 0 GT1+E0 H-1 0 GT1+E0 ZO1 CR GX0-E0 ZO1 CR
profile pgm along y BAND_X+BOSS-E0 H-1 0 BAND_X+BOSS+GP-LAND+E0 H-1 0
corner BAND_X+BOSS+GP-LAND+E0 ZO1 CR BAND_X+BOSS-E0 ZO1 CR
profile pgb along y GX0-E0 1 0 GX0-E0 ZO0 CR GB1+E0 ZO0 CR GB1+E0 1 0
profile pge along y GE0-E0 1 0 GE0-E0 ZO0 CR GE1+E0 ZO0 CR GE1+E0 1 0
extrude gt from YT to 0 pgt draft DRAFT pattern x 2 W-GT1-GX0
extrude gm from YT to 0 pgm draft DRAFT pattern x GN GP
extrude gb from YT to 0 pgb draft DRAFT pattern x 2 W-GB1-GX0
extrude ge from YT to 0 pge draft DRAFT pattern x 2 W-GE1-GE0
cut boot holed core gt gm gb ge

# The rounds.  Every edge that turns outward takes SOFT_R, but: the
# outer edge of the front, where the waves meet the outer faces, EDGE_R,
# up to the walls of the gap, the sides 9 and 19 of the profile; the
# rear edge of the lip opening on the ceiling of the recess, RECESS_R;
# the edges of the rear end, REAR_R, less than the round of the corners
# of the gap there; and the edges that stay sharp.  Those are the edges
# hidden in use: of the face against the panel, the two short ones where
# the recess meets the gap, the inner edges of the counterbore floors,
# under the screw heads, and the edges of the slots along the cavity.
# Sharp too are the crease on the parting line and the two ends of the
# sleeve's front part at the gap, which the rounds of its corners take
# whole.  The front ends of the grooves take
# FLOOR_R in their inner corners.
RECESS_R = 0.3
EDGE_R = 5.08
REAR_R = 0.5
FLOOR_R = 1.75
round SOFT_R convex
round EDGE_R sleeve.back.* wv.*
round EDGE_R sleeve.back.* wh.*
round SOFT_R sleeve.back.9 wh.*
round SOFT_R sleeve.back.19 wh.*
round RECESS_R tall.end *
round REAR_R rear.end *
sharp sleeve.back.* rear.backd.*
sharp sleeve.end *
sharp tall.end recess.lipx.*
sharp recess.end *
sharp sleeve.back.9 recess.lipx.*
sharp sleeve.back.19 recess.lipx.*
sharp cl*.end hl*
sharp cr*.start hr*
sharp ct*.start ht*
sharp cb*.end hb*
sharp sleeve.back.* k*
sharp rear.backd.* k*
sharp sleeve.back.* g*
sharp rear.backd.* g*
round FLOOR_R recess.end g*
